Recompute the flight estimate after RACK loss marking, exclude lost copies,
preserve loss/ACK flags on splits, and advance writeNext past fast repairs.
No RTO limits, retry budgets or congestion-control selection are changed.
The additional pkg/amnezia package exposes source/fix identifiers for build
verification. It does not alter transport behaviour.

This is a downstream backport of an open upstream proposal, not an assertion
of completed upstream review. Original gVisor copyrights and Apache-2.0
licensing remain in their source files and LICENSE. See the Amnezia tests
and revision lock for the scope and limits of validation.

Optional verified-path-probe-v1 API permits at most one additional payload repair per armed RTO deadline after a host-authenticated, sufficiently large bidirectional path challenge. It preserves ordinary timeout, retry, congestion and loss accounting. NeedsVerifiedPathProbe is a read-only scheduling hint. The host must bind proofs to network generation and expiry and enforce aggregate limits.
